---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DIGUP_UI } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title={'What Is DigUp? Local Multimodal File Search Explained'}
  description={'DigUp is an open-source, on-device app that finds photos, PDFs, documents, recordings, videos, and optional code by meaning using EmbeddingGemma 2 — not by filename alone.'}
  canonicalPath="/what-is-digup/"
  lang="en"
  ogImage={DIGUP_UI.multimodal.src}
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">Overview</span> · On-device semantic search</p>
      <h1>What is DigUp?</h1>
      <p class="lead">DigUp is a local-first multimodal semantic file search desktop app. You pick folders; it embeds what’s inside (photos, PDF pages, docs, audio windows, video frames, optional code) with EmbeddingGemma 2 and lets you search by meaning — on Mac, Windows, and Linux.</p>
      <ul class="job-steps" aria-label="Product job" style="margin-top:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <li><span class="n">1</span> Describe</li>
        <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
        <li><span class="n">2</span> Hit content</li>
        <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
        <li><span class="n">3</span> Open at location</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.4rem;margin:0;">
        <span class="mod-pill image">Images</span>
        <span class="mod-pill text">PDFs / docs</span>
        <span class="mod-pill audio">Audio</span>
        <span class="mod-pill video">Video</span>
        <span class="mod-pill code">Code (opt.)</span>
        <span class="mod-pill text">On-device</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="wide">

      <figure class="shot-panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <span class="shot-label">Real DigUp UI</span>
        <img src={DIGUP_UI.multimodal.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.multimodal.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="shot-caption">{DIGUP_UI.sourceNoteEn} Multimodal result list for “a dog on the beach.”</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>In one sentence</h2>
      <p>Describe what you remember about a file’s contents; DigUp ranks matches in a shared embedding space on your machine — no account, no cloud index of your files.</p>

      <h2>What it can search (modalities)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Modality</th>
            <th>What DigUp indexes</th>
            <th>Open-to</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Photos / images</strong></td>
            <td>Visual content (and OCR text on Mac for screenshots / scanned pages)</td>
            <td>File</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>PDFs</strong></td>
            <td>Pages as meaning + text; scanned PDFs get OCR on Mac (0.6.1+)</td>
            <td>Page</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Documents</strong></td>
            <td>txt, md, rtf, docx, odt, html; .doc mainly Mac</td>
            <td>File / passage</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Audio</strong></td>
            <td>~30-second windows in a shared vector space</td>
            <td>Timestamp</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Video</strong></td>
            <td>Frames / moments by description</td>
            <td>Timestamp</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Code (optional)</strong></td>
            <td>Enable in settings; query with <code>code:</code> prefix</td>
            <td>Line</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted">Win/Linux beta (0.7.0-beta.1) does not yet OCR screenshot text; skips old .doc, RAW, and SVG on that beta — see <a href="/install-windows/">Windows</a> / <a href="/install-linux/">Linux</a> guides.</p>

      <h2>How it works (high level)</h2>
      <ol class="checklist">
        <li><strong>You choose folders</strong> — DigUp does not auto-index the whole disk; cloud placeholders (undownloaded iCloud/OneDrive) are skipped.</li>
        <li><strong>Extract → embed</strong> — content becomes images/text/audio chunks; EmbeddingGemma 2 runs locally via llama.cpp (~865 MB first download).</li>
        <li><strong>SQLite index</strong> — vectors plus keyword boost for exact strings (invoice numbers, error codes, names).</li>
        <li><strong>Search</strong> — query text is embedded; nearest neighbors + keyword weights; hotkey opens the panel from any app.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>More on the model: <a href="/embeddinggemma-2/">How DigUp uses EmbeddingGemma 2</a>.</p>

      <h2>Requirements by platform</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Platform</th>
            <th>Version (2026-10-15)</th>
            <th>Hardware / OS</th>
            <th>Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Mac</strong></td>
            <td>0.6.1</td>
            <td>Apple Silicon, macOS 14+</td>
            <td>Stable</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Windows</strong></td>
            <td>0.7.0-beta.1</td>
            <td>64-bit Windows 10/11</td>
            <td><strong>Beta</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Linux</strong></td>
            <td>0.7.0-beta.1</td>
            <td>amd64; .deb or AppImage</td>
            <td><strong>Beta</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted">GitHub stars ~3,716 as of 2026-10-15 — re-check the <a href="https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp" rel="noopener noreferrer">repo</a> for live counts.</p>

      <h2>What DigUp is not</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Not a full Spotlight / Windows Search replacement (it can sit beside them).</li>
        <li>Not an app launcher (as of research date).</li>
        <li>Not a cloud sync or collaboration search product.</li>
        <li>Not available as an official App Store listing you should trust from random mirrors — use GitHub Releases.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-mac/">Mac install</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/vs-spotlight/">vs Spotlight</a>
      </div>

      <section class="related">
        <h2>Related</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <a class="card" href="/install-mac/"><h3>Install Mac</h3><p>Brew + DMG checklist</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/faq/"><h3>FAQ</h3><p>Privacy, platforms, troubleshooting</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/embeddinggemma-2/"><h3>EmbeddingGemma 2</h3><p>Model size and shared space</p></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
